  "notes": "{為|な}す is a literary/formal verb meaning 'to accomplish' or 'to do.' In modern speech, ⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧ is much more common.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: Transitive (⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧)\n- Pattern: X⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{為|な}す\n\nREGISTER: Literary/Formal\nThis verb is primarily used in formal writing, set expressions, and proverbs. It's rarely used in everyday conversation.\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- {為|な}すべき⟦こと→こと：01164_koto⟧ (what should be done)\n- {為|な}す⟦{術|すべ}→術：31699_sube⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧⟦ない→ない：01118_nai⟧ (to have no way to do anything)\n- 「{為|な}せば⟦{成|な}る→成る：01970_naru⟧」(Where there's a will, there's a way)\n\nWRITING:\n{為|な}す is the kanji for \"do\" ({為|な}すべきこと, {為|な}す⟦{術|すべ}→術：31699_sube⟧⟦も→も：00484_mo⟧⟦ない→ない：01118_nai⟧). For \"form, make up\" (⟦{列|れつ}→列：02171_retsu⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧なす, ⟦{意味|いみ}→意味：01155_imi⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧なさない) and for achieving something (⟦{名|な}→名：03496_na⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{成|な}す) the standard kanji is {成|な}す, and kana なす is common for both. The proverb {為|な}せば{成|な}る uses both kanji.",
